          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For a closed home office, the Levoit Dual 150 has the tank and output to raise the room's humidity and Levoit lists it under 28 dB. For a desk in a shared or open-plan office, a tabletop unit like the Pure Enrichment MistAire is the right size, with a nozzle you can aim away from electronics. Use distilled water near computers."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I run a humidifier from a USB port?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Some small humidifiers are designed to, but a standard USB 2.0 port supplies only about 2.5 watts and USB 3.0 about 4.5 watts, so USB-powered units have modest output. Rechargeable units may need a stronger charger: Canopy says its Portable needs a 10-watt USB-C charger. Check the power requirement on the listing before relying on a laptop port."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I bring a travel humidifier on a plane?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Generally yes, but carry it empty, because water in the tank counts as a liquid at security. If it has a built-in lithium battery, airlines usually want it in carry-on luggage rather than checked bags. Rules change and vary by airline, so check your carrier's current guidance before flying. Bottle-top designs avoid the water question entirely."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a small humidifier run on one tank?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on tank size and setting. Manufacturers quote run times on the lowest setting: the Levoit Dual 150 is listed at up to 25 hours from 3 liters, the MistAire Travel at up to six hours per 16.9-ounce bottle, and the Canopy Portable at up to 11 hours of battery on low. At higher output, expect noticeably less."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I use distilled water in a small humidifier?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In an ultrasonic humidifier, yes, if your tap water is hard or the unit sits near electronics. Ultrasonics turn dissolved minerals into white dust, and distilled water contains almost none. Distilled water also slows scale in the reservoir. Evaporative humidifiers trap minerals in the wick, so they handle tap water without dusting your desk."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are small humidifiers safe on a desk or nightstand?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cool-mist small humidifiers are generally safe on a desk or nightstand if they sit on a hard, waterproof surface and the mist is aimed into open air rather than at electronics, paper or wood. Keep them a couple of feet from the bed or keyboard, clean them every few days, and do not let the space go above about 50 percent humidity."
          }
        }
      ],
